      "sourceText": "27 credits of AMS courses numbered 301 and above, or approved non-AMS upper-division mathematically oriented courses, subject to the following constraints: AMS 301 must be taken; Either AMS 310 (Survey of Probability and Statistics) or AMS 311 (Probability Theory) must be taken; Either AMS 315 or AMS 361 or MAT 303 must be taken; At most 6 of the remaining 18 credits can be counted from the following courses: AMS 475, AMS 476, AMS 487, AMS 488, non-AMS upper division mathematically oriented courses. Typical non-AMS upper division mathematically oriented courses are ECO 321, ECO 348, CSE designated courses numbered 302 and above (excluding 312), and MAT designated courses numbered 310 and above."
