  "notes": [
    {
      "topic": "admission",
      "text": "Applications for major admission are reviewed twice per year and must be received by January 5 for Spring admission and June 5 for Fall admission. Admission requires either a grade of B- or better in calculus III (AMS 261 or MAT 203) and linear algebra (AMS 210 or MAT 211), or grades of C or better in both and a GPA of 2.8 or higher in these courses. At most one of the two courses may be repeated. Completed course evaluations are required for transferred courses used toward the major. AOI students must meet the requirements within one year of enrolling in the first course that applies toward major entry. Admission is competitive and contingent upon program capacity."
    },
    {
      "topic": "advising",
      "text": "Undergraduate Program Coordinator and Advisor: Amanda Sanger (ams_undergrad@stonybrook.edu). AMS majors may consider a double major or minor. Courses that apply toward both major requirements double count, and double majors must meet all AMS major requirements."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The AMS major covers the mathematical sciences topics tested in the first actuarial examination and part of the second. Students should see the Department's actuarial advisor for more information."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "Accelerated BS/MS (MS in AMS), accelerated BS in AMS / MS in DAS, and accelerated BS/MPH programs exist. These are not evaluated here; see the undergraduate program director and the graduate catalog."
    },
    {
      "topic": "sbc",
      "text": "The following AMS courses satisfy SBS+: AMS 316, 335, 341, and 342. The following AMS courses satisfy EXP+: AMS 333, 394, 412, 475, and 487. The following AMS courses satisfy ESI and CER: AMS 315, 394, and 412. The following AMS courses satisfy WRTD: AMS 300, 318, and 333. Consult the department for appropriate courses."
    }
  ],
